sangati kramanusara

  -- kramanusara: the rate of one quantity with respect to another (the krama axis)
  -- this is the general structure of d/dx — not only d/dt
  -- the krama axis is the denominator: can be time, distance, volume, angle, anything
  -- recursive: kramanusara of kramanusara is the second derivative (T^-2, etc.)
  -- each application adds -1 to the denominator dimension's SI exponent

  -- root structure: viveka is the act of differentiation (discerning the instant)
  -- sama-kalana is integration (gathering the whole) — kramanusara is the inverse direction
  "viveka-abheda sama-kalana-pratipaksha"

  "krama-sthita tat-kshana-siddha"
  "purva-rupa-sthita uttara-rupa-phala"
  "matra-janya vivartana-kriya"
  "svayambhu-yukta"

  -- svayambhu-yukta: self-composable — kramanusara of kramanusara is valid (2nd derivative etc.)
  -- matra-janya: produces a new unit by dividing numerator dim by denominator dim

shabda rate-of-one-thing-wrt-another / the-d-by-dx-structure-viveka-at-each-instant-the-krama-axis-is-the-denominator-recursive-each-application-subtracts-one-from-that-dimensions-exponent

